IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgk-div8-application`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 4 Division 8, ss 131 to 133: registration of charges, the duty to register, and the duty to register charges existing on acquired property.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. The time limits of ss 131 and 133 take the s 139 extension from sgk-div8-application.l4.
-- The Registrar and the Court appear only as what their acts mean to the person; s 137 (the Court's relief) is in sgk-div8-register.l4,
-- and its result enters here as two plain inputs (the Court has extended the time; the day to which it extended it).
-- Marks in the comments: "FALSE-kind" and "NOTHING-kind" say why a branch answers JUST FALSE or NOTHING; "fork F-Kn" points at the fork register of NOTES.md.

§ `The nouns of ss 131 to 133`

-- What a witness can say about a charge, field by field from s 131(3) to (3C) and (11). It carries no rule.
DECLARE `s 131(3) the facts about the charge` HAS
    `the charge was created by a company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the charge was created` IS A DATE
    `the charge secures an issue of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the charge is on uncalled share capital of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the charge is on shares of a subsidiary of a company which are owned by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument which, if executed by an individual, would require registration as a bill of sale` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the charge is on land wherever situate or on an interest in land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the charge is for a rent or other periodical sum issuing out of land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the charge is on book debts of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the charge is on a negotiable instrument or on debentures issued by the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the charge is a floating charge on the undertaking or property of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the charge is on calls made but not paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the charge is on a ship or aircraft or any share in a ship or aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the charge is on goodwill, a patent, a trade mark, a copyright or a registered design, or on a licence under or to use any of them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the charge is capable of being registered under the International Interests in Aircraft Equipment Act 2009` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the charge was one to which section 131 applied under subsection (3) as in force immediately before 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the charge is a shipowner's lien` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on 1 October 2018 an order for the winding up of the company had been made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on 1 October 2018 a resolution had been passed for the voluntary winding up of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on 1 October 2018 a creditor of the company had acquired a proprietary right to or an interest in the subject matter of the lien` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The acts that the regulative rules of ss 131 to 133 name.
DECLARE `s 131 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 131(1) lodge with the Registrar a statement containing the prescribed particulars of the charge`
    `s 131(6) lodge with the Registrar the particulars of the date and amount of an issue of debentures`
    `s 133(1) lodge with the Registrar a statement of the prescribed particulars of the charge`

-- The paragraphs of s 133(1).
DECLARE `s 133(1) paragraph` IS ONE OF
    `s 133(1)(a) a company acquires property subject to a charge`
    `s 133(1)(b) a foreign company becomes registered after creating a charge`
    `s 133(1)(c) a foreign company becomes registered after acquiring property subject to a charge`

§ `Section 131(3), (3A) to (3C) and (11): the charges to which section 131 applies`

-- src:11224 | (11) In this section, “shipowner’s lien” means a contractual lien
-- src:11225 | on —
-- src:11227 | (a) sub‑freights;
-- src:11229 | (b) sub‑hires; or
-- src:11231 | (c) bill of lading freight,
-- src:11233 | created under a charter (or sub‑charter) of a ship for any amount due
-- src:11234 | under the charter (or sub‑charter).
@ref s 131(11) (src:11224-11234)
GIVEN `the lien is a contractual lien` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lien is on sub-freights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lien is on sub-hires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lien is on bill of lading freight` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lien is created under a charter (or sub-charter) of a ship for any amount due under the charter (or sub-charter)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(11) the lien is a shipowner's lien` MEANS
    IF    `the lien is a contractual lien`
       AND (`the lien is on sub-freights` OR `the lien is on sub-hires` OR `the lien is on bill of lading freight`)
       AND `the lien is created under a charter (or sub-charter) of a ship for any amount due under the charter (or sub-charter)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section, “shipowner’s lien” means a contractual lien on — (a) sub-freights; (b) sub-hires; or (c) bill of lading freight, created under a charter (or sub-charter) of a ship for any amount due under the charter (or sub-charter)"

-- src:11066 | (3) This section applies to the following charges that are created on
-- src:11067 | or after 3 January 2016:
-- src:11069 | (a) a charge to secure any issue of debentures;
-- src:11071 | (b) a charge on uncalled share capital of a company;
-- src:11073 | (c) a charge on shares of a subsidiary of a company which are
-- src:11074 | owned by the company;
-- src:11076 | (d) a charge created or evidenced by an instrument which if
-- src:11077 | executed by an individual, would require registration as a
-- src:11078 | bill of sale;
-- src:11080 | (e) a charge on land wherever situate or any interest therein
-- src:11081 | but not including any charge for any rent or other
-- src:11082 | periodical sum issuing out of land;
-- src:11084 | (f) a charge on book debts of the company;
-- src:11089 | (g) a floating charge on the undertaking or property of a
-- src:11090 | company;
-- src:11092 | (h) a charge on calls made but not paid;
-- src:11094 | (i) a charge on a ship or aircraft or any share in a ship or
-- src:11095 | aircraft;
-- src:11097 | (j) a charge on goodwill, on a patent or a licence under a
-- src:11098 | patent, on a trade mark or a licence to use a trademark, or
-- src:11099 | on a copyright or a licence under a copyright or on a
-- src:11100 | registered design or a licence to use a registered design.
@ref s 131(3) (src:11066-11100)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 131(3) the facts about the charge`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 131(3) the charge falls within one of paragraphs (a) to (j)` MEANS
       facts's `the charge secures an issue of debentures`                                                                                  -- (a)
    OR facts's `the charge is on uncalled share capital of a company`                                                                       -- (b)
    OR facts's `the charge is on shares of a subsidiary of a company which are owned by the company`                                        -- (c)
    OR facts's `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument which, if executed by an individual, would require registration as a bill of sale`   -- (d)
    OR (facts's `the charge is on land wherever situate or on an interest in land` AND (NOT facts's `the charge is for a rent or other periodical sum issuing out of land`))   -- (e) "but not including any charge for any rent or other periodical sum issuing out of land"
    OR (facts's `the charge is on book debts of the company` AND (NOT facts's `the charge is on a negotiable instrument or on debentures issued by the Government`))        -- (f) with s 131(3A)
    OR facts's `the charge is a floating charge on the undertaking or property of the company`                                              -- (g)
    OR facts's `the charge is on calls made but not paid`                                                                                   -- (h)
    OR facts's `the charge is on a ship or aircraft or any share in a ship or aircraft`                                                     -- (i)
    OR facts's `the charge is on goodwill, a patent, a trade mark, a copyright or a registered design, or on a licence under or to use any of them`   -- (j)

-- src:11104 | (3AA) This section also applies to any charge that —
-- src:11106 | (a) was a charge to which this section applied under
-- src:11107 | subsection (3) in force immediately before 3 January
-- src:11108 | 2016; and
-- src:11110 | (b) was created before that date.
-- src:11112 | [36/2014]
-- src:11114 | (3AB) Despite subsection (3), a shipowner’s lien created by a
-- src:11115 | company on or after 1 October 2018, whether as a charge on book
-- src:11116 | debts of the company or a floating charge on the undertaking or
-- src:11117 | property of the company, is not a charge to which this section applies.
-- src:11119 | [35/2018]
-- src:11121 | (3AC) Despite subsection (3) or (3AA), a shipowner’s lien created
-- src:11122 | by a company before 1 October 2018, whether as a charge on book
-- src:11123 | debts of the company or a floating charge on the undertaking or
-- src:11124 | property of the company, is a charge to which this section applies only
-- src:11125 | if, as at that date —
-- src:11127 | (a) an order for the winding up of the company has been made;
-- src:11129 | (b) a resolution has been passed for the voluntary winding up
-- src:11130 | of the company; or
-- src:11132 | (c) a creditor of the company has acquired a proprietary right
-- src:11133 | to or an interest in the subject matter of the lien.
-- src:11135 | [35/2018]
-- src:11137 | (3A) The reference to a charge on book debts in subsection (3)(f)
-- src:11138 | does not include a reference to a charge on a negotiable instrument or
-- src:11139 | on debentures issued by the Government.
-- src:11144 | (3B) A charge mentioned in subsection (3) does not include a
-- src:11145 | charge created at any time on or after 1 May 2009 to the extent that it
-- src:11146 | is capable of being registered under the International Interests in
-- src:11147 | Aircraft Equipment Act 2009.
-- src:11149 | [5/2009]
-- src:11151 | (3C) In subsection (3B), “registered” has the meaning given by
-- src:11152 | section 2(1) of the International Interests in Aircraft Equipment
-- src:11153 | Act 2009.
-- src:11155 | [5/2009]
@ref s 131(3AA) to (3C) (src:11104-11155)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 131(3) the facts about the charge`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(3) the charge is one to which section 131 applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT facts's `the charge was created by a company`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 131(1) speaks of "a charge to which this section applies is created by a company"; it says nothing of a charge created by anyone else
        IF facts's `the charge is a shipowner's lien` AND facts's `the day the charge was created` AT LEAST Date 1 10 2018
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a shipowner’s lien created by a company on or after 1 October 2018 ... is not a charge to which this section applies" (s 131(3AB))
        IF facts's `the charge is a shipowner's lien` AND facts's `the day the charge was created` LESS THAN Date 1 10 2018
           AND (NOT (facts's `on 1 October 2018 an order for the winding up of the company had been made` OR facts's `on 1 October 2018 a resolution had been passed for the voluntary winding up of the company` OR facts's `on 1 October 2018 a creditor of the company had acquired a proprietary right to or an interest in the subject matter of the lien`))
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a shipowner’s lien created by a company before 1 October 2018 ... is a charge to which this section applies only if, as at that date — (a) an order for the winding up ... (b) a resolution ... (c) a creditor ..." (s 131(3AC), "only if")
        IF facts's `the day the charge was created` AT LEAST `the day 3 January 2016`
        THEN (IF `s 131(3) the charge falls within one of paragraphs (a) to (j)` facts
              THEN (IF facts's `the charge is capable of being registered under the International Interests in Aircraft Equipment Act 2009` AND facts's `the day the charge was created` AT LEAST Date 1 5 2009
                    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A charge mentioned in subsection (3) does not include a charge created at any time on or after 1 May 2009 to the extent that it is capable of being registered under the International Interests in Aircraft Equipment Act 2009" (s 131(3B); fork F-K3)
                    ELSE JUST TRUE)
              ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): section 131(3) says it "applies to the following charges"; it does not say it applies to no other charge
        IF facts's `the charge was one to which section 131 applied under subsection (3) as in force immediately before 3 January 2016`
        THEN JUST TRUE    -- s 131(3AA): "This section also applies to any charge that — (a) was a charge to which this section applied under subsection (3) in force immediately before 3 January 2016; and (b) was created before that date"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the subsection (3) in force before 3 January 2016 is not in this text, so a charge created before that date that the fact above does not cover is outside what this text says

§ `Section 131(1): the statement, the time, and what follows if it is not lodged`

-- The rule as a plain period test: "within 30 days after the creation of the charge" (the s 139 extension for a document made out of Singapore included).
-- src:11043 | 131.—(1) Subject to this Division, where a charge to which this
-- src:11044 | section applies is created by a company there must be lodged with the
-- src:11045 | Registrar in the prescribed manner for registration, within 30 days
-- src:11046 | after the creation of the charge, a statement containing the prescribed
-- src:11047 | particulars of the charge, and if this section is not complied with in
-- src:11048 | relation to the charge the charge is, so far as any security on the
-- src:11049 | company’s property or undertaking is thereby conferred, void against
-- src:11050 | the liquidator and any creditor of the company.
@ref s 131(1) (src:11043-11050)
GIVEN `the day the charge was created` IS A DATE
      `the day the statement was lodged` IS A DATE
      `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of further days the Registrar has allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 131(1) the statement is lodged within 30 days after the creation of the charge` MEANS
    `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the charge was created` `the day the statement was lodged`
        (30 PLUS `s 139 the number of days added to the time specified` `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore` `the number of further days the Registrar has allowed`)
        Days     -- fork F-K4: "within 30 days after" read as a deadline: lodging on or before the 30th day is in time, the day of creation included

-- "there must be lodged ... a statement": the duty as a decision. The text's gate is "where a charge to which this section applies is created by a company".
@ref s 131(1) (src:11043-11050)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 131(3) the facts about the charge`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(1) a statement of the charge must be lodged with the Registrar` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 131(3) the charge is one to which section 131 applies` facts
    WHEN JUST applies THEN JUST applies    -- JUST FALSE here is the text's no: a charge that section 131(3AB), (3AC) or (3B) takes out; a gate unmet is "where", the provision's own question (fork F-K5)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING              -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): section 131(3) does not say whether this charge is one to which the section applies

-- "void against the liquidator and any creditor": the effect of not complying. "Subject to this Division": s 139 (time) and s 137 (the Court's extension) enter as inputs.
@ref s 131(1) (src:11043-11050)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 131(3) the facts about the charge`
      `the statement of the charge has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the statement was lodged` IS A DATE
      `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of further days the Registrar has allowed` IS A NUMBER
      `the Court has by order under section 137 extended the time for registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day to which the Court has extended the time for registration` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(1) the security the charge confers is void against the liquidator and any creditor of the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 131(3) the charge is one to which section 131 applies` facts
    WHEN JUST applies THEN
        IF applies
        THEN (IF    `the statement of the charge has been lodged with the Registrar`
                AND (   `s 131(1) the statement is lodged within 30 days after the creation of the charge` (facts's `the day the charge was created`) `the day the statement was lodged` `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore` `the number of further days the Registrar has allowed`
                     OR (`the Court has by order under section 137 extended the time for registration` AND `the day the statement was lodged` AT MOST `the last day to which the Court has extended the time for registration`))
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): voidness is imposed "if this section is not complied with in relation to the charge"; the section was complied with (an "if" unmet: marginal reading (a))
              ELSE JUST TRUE)
        ELSE JUST FALSE         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the provision applies "where a charge to which this section applies is created by a company"; the charge is not one to which it applies (a "where" unmet: periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): section 131(3) does not say whether the section applies to this charge

-- The duty as a regulative rule. The text says "there must be lodged" and names no one; s 132(1) puts the default on the company and its officers,
-- so the company is the party taken here (fork F-K6). The consequence of a missed day is the voidness above and the offence of s 132(1).
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the number of days by which section 139 extends the time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 131 act`
`s 131(1) the company must lodge the statement of the charge within 30 days after the creation of the charge` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 131(1) lodge with the Registrar a statement containing the prescribed particulars of the charge`
    WITHIN (30 PLUS `the number of days by which section 139 extends the time`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the statement of the charge was not lodged with the Registrar within 30 days after the creation of the charge"

§ `Section 131(1A): production of the instrument`

-- src:11054 | (1A) In connection with the registration of a charge to which this
-- src:11055 | section applies which is created by a company there must be produced
-- src:11056 | to the Registrar, upon the Registrar’s request and for the purposes of
-- src:11057 | inspection, at no cost to the Registrar, the instrument (if any) by
-- src:11058 | which the charge is created or evidenced or a certified true copy
-- src:11059 | thereof.
@ref s 131(1A) (src:11054-11059)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 131(3) the facts about the charge`
      `the Registrar has requested production of the instrument for the purposes of inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(1A) the instrument or a certified true copy must be produced to the Registrar` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 131(3) the charge is one to which section 131 applies` facts
    WHEN JUST applies THEN
        IF applies AND `the Registrar has requested production of the instrument for the purposes of inspection`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the duty arises "upon the Registrar’s request" in connection with "a charge to which this section applies"; without the request, or without such a charge, it does not arise (an "upon" unmet: periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (b) and (c); fork F-K5)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): section 131(3) does not say whether the section applies to this charge

@ref s 131(1A) (src:11054-11059)
GIVEN `the amount the Registrar is charged for the production` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(1A) the production is at no cost to the Registrar` MEANS
    IF `the amount the Registrar is charged for the production` EQUALS 0
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the production must be "at no cost to the Registrar"

§ `Section 131(2): the contract stands, and the money secured falls due`

-- src:11061 | (2) Nothing in subsection (1) affects any contract or obligation for
-- src:11062 | repayment of the money secured by a charge and when a charge
-- src:11063 | becomes void under this section the money secured thereby
-- src:11064 | immediately becomes payable.
@ref s 131(2) (src:11061-11064)
GIVEN `the contract or obligation is one for repayment of the money secured by the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(2) subsection (1) affects the contract or obligation` MEANS
    IF `the contract or obligation is one for repayment of the money secured by the charge`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in subsection (1) affects any contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by a charge"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about a contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured

@ref s 131(2) (src:11061-11064)
GIVEN `the charge has become void under section 131` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(2) the money secured by the charge becomes immediately payable by force of this subsection` MEANS
    IF `the charge has become void under section 131`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the money becomes immediately payable "when a charge becomes void under this section"; a "when" unmet (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (b) and (c); the name says "by force of this subsection", so the answer is not that the money cannot fall due on another ground)

§ `Section 131(4): a charge on property outside Singapore`

-- src:11157 | (4) Where a charge created in Singapore affects property outside
-- src:11158 | Singapore, the statement containing the prescribed particulars of the
-- src:11159 | charge may be lodged for registration under and in accordance with
-- src:11160 | subsection (1) even though further proceedings may be necessary to
-- src:11161 | make the charge valid or effectual according to the law of the place in
-- src:11162 | which the property is situate.
@ref s 131(4) (src:11157-11162)
GIVEN `the charge was created in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge affects property outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(4) the statement may be lodged even though further proceedings are necessary under the law of the place where the property is` MEANS
    IF `the charge was created in Singapore` AND `the charge affects property outside Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection begins "Where a charge created in Singapore affects property outside Singapore"; a "may" gated by "where" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork F-K7, the grant and the periods rulings point two ways)

§ `Section 131(5) to (8): a series of debentures, and a commission, allowance or discount`

-- src:11164 | (5) When a series of debentures containing or giving by reference to
-- src:11165 | any other instrument any charge to the benefit of which the debenture
-- src:11166 | holders of that series are entitled equally is created by a company, it is
-- src:11167 | sufficient if there is lodged with the Registrar for registration within
-- src:11168 | 30 days after the execution of the instrument containing the charge, or
-- src:11169 | if there is no such instrument after the execution of the first debenture
-- src:11170 | of the series, a statement containing the following particulars:
-- src:11172 | (a) the total amount secured by the whole series;
-- src:11174 | (b) the dates of the resolutions authorising the issue of the
-- src:11175 | series and the date of the covering instrument (if any) by
-- src:11176 | which the security is created or defined;
-- src:11178 | (c) a general description of the property charged;
-- src:11180 | (d) the names of the trustee (if any) for the debenture holders.
@ref s 131(5) (src:11164-11180)
GIVEN `the debentures are a series giving by reference to an instrument a charge to the benefit of which the debenture holders of the series are entitled equally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the instrument containing the charge was executed, or the first debenture of the series if there is no such instrument` IS A DATE
      `the day the statement was lodged` IS A DATE
      `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of further days the Registrar has allowed` IS A NUMBER
      `the statement gives the total amount secured by the whole series` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives the dates of the resolutions authorising the issue of the series and the date of the covering instrument (if any)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives a general description of the property charged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives the names of the trustee (if any) for the debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(5) the lodging of the statement is sufficient` MEANS
    IF    `the debentures are a series giving by reference to an instrument a charge to the benefit of which the debenture holders of the series are entitled equally`
       AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the instrument containing the charge was executed, or the first debenture of the series if there is no such instrument` `the day the statement was lodged`
              (30 PLUS `s 139 the number of days added to the time specified` `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore` `the number of further days the Registrar has allowed`) Days
       AND `the statement gives the total amount secured by the whole series`
       AND `the statement gives the dates of the resolutions authorising the issue of the series and the date of the covering instrument (if any)`
       AND `the statement gives a general description of the property charged`
       AND `the statement gives the names of the trustee (if any) for the debenture holders`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is sufficient if there is lodged ... within 30 days ... a statement containing the following particulars" (an "if" unmet: marginal reading (a); fork F-K8)

-- src:11182 | (6) For the purposes of subsection (5), where more than one issue is
-- src:11183 | made of debentures in the series, there must be lodged within 30 days
-- src:11184 | after each issue particulars of the date and amount of each issue, but
-- src:11185 | an omission to do so does not affect the validity of the debentures
-- src:11186 | issued.
@ref s 131(6) (src:11182-11186)
GIVEN `the day of the issue` IS A DATE
      `the day the particulars were lodged` IS A DATE
      `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of further days the Registrar has allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 131(6) the particulars of the issue are lodged within 30 days after the issue` MEANS
    `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day of the issue` `the day the particulars were lodged`
        (30 PLUS `s 139 the number of days added to the time specified` `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore` `the number of further days the Registrar has allowed`)
        Days     -- fork F-K4

@ref s 131(6) (src:11182-11186)
GIVEN `the particulars of the date and amount of an issue were not lodged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(6) the omission affects the validity of the debentures issued` MEANS
    IF `the particulars of the date and amount of an issue were not lodged`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an omission to do so does not affect the validity of the debentures issued"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks of an omission; where nothing was omitted it says nothing of validity

-- The duty as a regulative rule: where more than one issue is made in the series, particulars must be lodged within 30 days after each issue.
-- The text says "there must be lodged" and names no one; the company is the party taken (fork F-K6).
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the number of days by which section 139 extends the time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 131 act`
`s 131(6) the company must lodge the particulars of each issue within 30 days after it` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 131(6) lodge with the Registrar the particulars of the date and amount of an issue of debentures`
    WITHIN (30 PLUS `the number of days by which section 139 extends the time`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the particulars of the date and amount of an issue of debentures were not lodged within 30 days after the issue"

-- src:11188 | (7) Where any commission, allowance or discount has been paid or
-- src:11189 | made either directly or indirectly by a company to any person in
-- src:11194 | consideration of the person (whether absolutely or conditionally)
-- src:11195 | subscribing or agreeing to subscribe or procuring or agreeing to
-- src:11196 | procure subscriptions, whether absolute or conditional, for any
-- src:11197 | debentures, the particulars required to be lodged under this section
-- src:11198 | must include particulars as to the amount or rate per cent of the
-- src:11199 | commission, allowance or discount so paid or made, but omission to
-- src:11200 | do so does not affect the validity of the debentures issued.
@ref s 131(7) (src:11188-11200)
GIVEN `a commission, allowance or discount has been paid or made, directly or indirectly, by the company to a person in consideration of the person subscribing or agreeing to subscribe, or procuring or agreeing to procure subscriptions, for debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(7) the particulars required to be lodged must include the amount or rate per cent of the commission, allowance or discount` MEANS
    IF `a commission, allowance or discount has been paid or made, directly or indirectly, by the company to a person in consideration of the person subscribing or agreeing to subscribe, or procuring or agreeing to procure subscriptions, for debentures`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the requirement arises "where any commission, allowance or discount has been paid or made"; a "where" unmet (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork F-K5)

@ref s 131(7) (src:11188-11200)
GIVEN `the particulars of the commission, allowance or discount were omitted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(7) the omission affects the validity of the debentures issued` MEANS
    IF `the particulars of the commission, allowance or discount were omitted`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "omission to do so does not affect the validity of the debentures issued"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks of an omission; where nothing was omitted it says nothing of validity

-- src:11202 | (8) The deposit of any debentures as security for any debt of the
-- src:11203 | company is not for the purposes of subsection (7) to be treated as the
-- src:11204 | issue of the debentures at a discount.
@ref s 131(8) (src:11202-11204)
GIVEN `the debentures are deposited as security for a debt of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(8) the deposit is treated as the issue of the debentures at a discount for the purposes of subsection (7)` MEANS
    IF `the debentures are deposited as security for a debt of the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The deposit of any debentures as security for any debt of the company is not for the purposes of subsection (7) to be treated as the issue of the debentures at a discount"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about the deposit of debentures as security for a debt of the company

§ `Section 131(9): no other registration`

-- src:11206 | (9) No charge or assignment to which this section applies (except a
-- src:11207 | charge or assignment relating to land) need be filed or registered
-- src:11208 | under any other written law.
@ref s 131(9) (src:11206-11208)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 131(3) the facts about the charge`
      `the charge or assignment relates to land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(9) the charge or assignment needs to be filed or registered under another written law` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 131(3) the charge is one to which section 131 applies` facts
    WHEN JUST applies THEN
        IF applies AND (NOT `the charge or assignment relates to land`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No charge or assignment to which this section applies (except a charge or assignment relating to land) need be filed or registered under any other written law"
        ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence leaves out a charge or assignment relating to land and speaks only of one to which the section applies
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): section 131(3) does not say whether the section applies to this charge

§ `Section 131(10): a second charge for the same debt within 30 days of a prior unregistered charge`

-- src:11210 | (10) Where a charge requiring registration under this section is
-- src:11211 | created before the lapse of 30 days after the creation of a prior
-- src:11212 | unregistered charge, and comprises all or any part of the property
-- src:11213 | comprised in the prior charge, and the subsequent charge is given as a
-- src:11214 | security for the same debt as is secured by the prior charge, or any part
-- src:11215 | of that debt, then to the extent to which the subsequent charge is a
-- src:11216 | security for the same debt or part thereof, and so far as respects the
-- src:11217 | property comprised in the prior charge, the subsequent charge is not
-- src:11218 | operative and does not have any validity unless it is proved to the
-- src:11219 | satisfaction of the Court that it was given in good faith for the purpose
-- src:11220 | of correcting some material error in the prior charge or under other
-- src:11221 | proper circumstances and not for the purposes of avoiding or evading
-- src:11222 | the provisions of this Division.
@ref s 131(10) (src:11210-11222)
GIVEN `the subsequent charge requires registration under section 131` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subsequent charge was created before the lapse of 30 days after the creation of a prior unregistered charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subsequent charge comprises all or part of the property comprised in the prior charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subsequent charge is given as security for the same debt as the prior charge, or any part of that debt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved to the satisfaction of the Court that the subsequent charge was given in good faith for the purpose of correcting some material error in the prior charge or under other proper circumstances and not for the purposes of avoiding or evading the provisions of Division 8` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(10) the subsequent charge is not operative and has no validity as respects the property comprised in the prior charge` MEANS
    IF    `the subsequent charge requires registration under section 131`
       AND `the subsequent charge was created before the lapse of 30 days after the creation of a prior unregistered charge`
       AND `the subsequent charge comprises all or part of the property comprised in the prior charge`
       AND `the subsequent charge is given as security for the same debt as the prior charge, or any part of that debt`
    THEN (IF `it is proved to the satisfaction of the Court that the subsequent charge was given in good faith for the purpose of correcting some material error in the prior charge or under other proper circumstances and not for the purposes of avoiding or evading the provisions of Division 8`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsequent charge is not operative "unless it is proved to the satisfaction of the Court" that it was given in good faith; an "unless" met (fork F-K9)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE JUST FALSE         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection applies "where a charge requiring registration ... is created before the lapse of 30 days after the creation of a prior unregistered charge" and the other conditions; a "where" unmet (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b))

§ `Section 132: who may lodge, the offence, and the fees`

-- src:11243 | 132.—(1) Documents and particulars required to be lodged for
-- src:11244 | registration in accordance with section 131 may be lodged for
-- src:11245 | registration in the prescribed manner by the company concerned or by
-- src:11246 | any person interested in the documents, but if default is made in
-- src:11247 | complying with that section the company and every officer of the
-- src:11248 | company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:11249 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000 and also to a
-- src:11250 | default penalty.
@ref s 132(1) (src:11243-11250)
GIVEN `the person is the company concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person interested in the documents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 132(1) the person may lodge the documents and particulars for registration` MEANS
    IF `the person is the company concerned` OR `the person is a person interested in the documents`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection names the company concerned and "any person interested in the documents"; it does not say that no one else may lodge them

@ref s 132(1) (src:11243-11250)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 131` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 132(1) the person is guilty of the offence of default in complying with section 131` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 131` AND (`the person is the company concerned` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): an element of the offence is unmet ("if default is made in complying with that section the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence"); the provision's own question (split site (i); fork F-K10)

@ref s 132(1) (src:11243-11250)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 131` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 132(1) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 131` AND (`the person is the company concerned` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase`)
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 1000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- "a fine not exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty": no imprisonment, so no term to combine with the fine
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is fixed only for a person the subsection makes guilty

-- src:11254 | (2) Where registration is effected by some person other than the
-- src:11255 | company, that person is entitled to recover from the company the
-- src:11256 | amount of any fees properly paid by the person on the registration.
@ref s 132(2) (src:11254-11256)
GIVEN `the registration is effected by a person other than the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fees were properly paid by that person on the registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 132(2) the person is entitled to recover the fees from the company` MEANS
    IF `the registration is effected by a person other than the company` AND `the fees were properly paid by that person on the registration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the entitlement arises "where registration is effected by some person other than the company" and for "fees properly paid"; a "where" unmet (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)); an "entitled"-named function the Guide leaves open (fork F-K11)

@ref s 132(2) (src:11254-11256)
GIVEN `the registration is effected by a person other than the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the fees properly paid by the person on the registration, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 132(2) the amount the person may recover from the company` MEANS
    IF `the registration is effected by a person other than the company`
    THEN JUST `the amount of the fees properly paid by the person on the registration, in Singapore dollars`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection fixes an amount only where registration is effected by a person other than the company

§ `Section 133: charges existing on property acquired, and a foreign company that becomes registered`

-- src:11261 | 133.—(1) Where —
-- src:11263 | (a) a company acquires any property which is subject to a
-- src:11264 | charge of any such kind as would, if it had been created by
-- src:11265 | the company after the acquisition of the property, have
-- src:11266 | been required to be registered under this Division;
-- src:11268 | (b) a foreign company becomes registered in Singapore and
-- src:11269 | has prior to such registration created a charge which if it
-- src:11270 | had been created by the company while it was registered in
-- src:11271 | Singapore would have been required to be registered under
-- src:11272 | this Division; or
-- src:11274 | (c) a foreign company becomes registered in Singapore and
-- src:11275 | has prior to such registration acquired property which is
-- src:11276 | subject to a charge of any such kind as would if it had been
-- src:11277 | created by the company after the acquisition and while it
-- src:11278 | was registered in Singapore have been required to be
-- src:11279 | registered under this Division,
-- src:11281 | the company must cause a statement of the prescribed particulars to
-- src:11282 | be lodged with the Registrar for registration within 30 days after the
-- src:11283 | date on which the acquisition is completed or the date of the
-- src:11284 | registration of the company in Singapore, as the case may be.
@ref s 133(1) (src:11261-11284)
GIVEN `the company acquires property which is subject to a charge of a kind that would have required registration under Division 8 had the company created it after the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a foreign company becomes registered in Singapore and has before its registration created a charge that would have required registration under Division 8 had it been created while the company was registered in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a foreign company becomes registered in Singapore and has before its registration acquired property subject to a charge that would have required registration under Division 8 had the property been acquired while the company was registered in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 133(1) the company must cause a statement of the prescribed particulars of the charge to be lodged with the Registrar` MEANS
    IF    `the company acquires property which is subject to a charge of a kind that would have required registration under Division 8 had the company created it after the acquisition`
       OR `a foreign company becomes registered in Singapore and has before its registration created a charge that would have required registration under Division 8 had it been created while the company was registered in Singapore`
       OR `a foreign company becomes registered in Singapore and has before its registration acquired property subject to a charge that would have required registration under Division 8 had the property been acquired while the company was registered in Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the duty arises "where" one of paragraphs (a) to (c) holds; a "where" unmet on a duty (fork F-K5)

@ref s 133(1) (src:11261-11284)
GIVEN paragraph IS A `s 133(1) paragraph`
      `the day the acquisition is completed` IS A DATE
      `the day the foreign company is registered in Singapore` IS A DATE
      `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of further days the Registrar has allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 133(1) the last day for lodging the statement` MEANS
    `s 139 the last day for lodging the document`
        (CONSIDER paragraph
         WHEN `s 133(1)(a) a company acquires property subject to a charge` THEN `the day the acquisition is completed`
         WHEN `s 133(1)(b) a foreign company becomes registered after creating a charge` THEN `the day the foreign company is registered in Singapore`
         WHEN `s 133(1)(c) a foreign company becomes registered after acquiring property subject to a charge` THEN `the day the foreign company is registered in Singapore`)
        30
        `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore`
        `the number of further days the Registrar has allowed`
        -- fork F-K12: "the date on which the acquisition is completed or the date of the registration ..., as the case may be": paragraph (a) runs from the acquisition, (b) and (c) from the registration

@ref s 133(1) (src:11261-11284)
GIVEN paragraph IS A `s 133(1) paragraph`
      `the day the acquisition is completed` IS A DATE
      `the day the foreign company is registered in Singapore` IS A DATE
      `the day the statement was lodged` IS A DATE
      `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of further days the Registrar has allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 133(1) the statement is lodged within 30 days after the date` MEANS
    `the day the statement was lodged` AT MOST
        `s 133(1) the last day for lodging the statement` paragraph `the day the acquisition is completed` `the day the foreign company is registered in Singapore`
            `the document was executed or made in a place out of Singapore` `the number of further days the Registrar has allowed`

-- The duty as a regulative rule. The party is the company, or the foreign company that has become registered ("the company must cause").
GIVEN party IS A Party
      `the number of days by which section 139 extends the time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 131 act`
`s 133(1) the company must cause the statement to be lodged within 30 days` MEANS
    PARTY party
    MUST `s 133(1) lodge with the Registrar a statement of the prescribed particulars of the charge`
    WITHIN (30 PLUS `the number of days by which section 139 extends the time`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY party BECAUSE "the statement of the prescribed particulars was not lodged within 30 days after the acquisition was completed or the company was registered in Singapore"

-- src:11289 | (2) If default is made in complying with this section, the company
-- src:11290 | or the foreign company and every officer of the company or foreign
-- src:11291 | company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:11292 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000 and also to a
-- src:11293 | default penalty.
@ref s 133(2) (src:11289-11293)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 133` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company or the foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 133(2) the person is guilty of the offence of default in complying with section 133` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 133` AND (`the person is the company or the foreign company` OR `the person is an officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): an element of the offence is unmet ("If default is made in complying with this section, the company or the foreign company and every officer ... who is in default shall be guilty of an offence"); split site (i); fork F-K10

@ref s 133(2) (src:11289-11293)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 133` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company or the foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 133(2) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 133` AND (`the person is the company or the foreign company` OR `the person is an officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase`)
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 1000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- "a fine not exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is fixed only for a person the subsection makes guilty
